      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T07:47:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/btm/btm_sec.cc;drc\u003d50f7acaf28c3847bcb59f65e6ad3b25d7e7e1e49;l\u003d3462\n\nHi Himanshu, if I understand correctly the snippet shows that LibBluetooth doesn\u0027t start a SMP if the bond is temporary. But the issue we met is:\n1. LibBluetooth started an outgoing temporary connection to BlueZ\n2. BlueZ noticed that the remote is a dual device so started a SMP\n3. LibBluetooth generated the LTK but eventually dropped the key on BTA_DM_BLE_AUTH_CMPL_EVT\n4. However, the sec_flags is not cleared for LE",
      "parentUuid": "0e482d61_1ddc6ead",
      "revId": "f8c20e81dc5a462546c8daa02d98cca4b64e4112",
